================================================================================
r141 -- size r140 option (a): consumer-side honest-algebra re-gate
RAN (executed on-box). Provenance audited line-by-line against md5 before
owner review.
================================================================================

SETUP
  Secure-8192 (N=19/T=9 L=2 H=14), nargo beta.26 + bb 5.1.0, 4-core.
  6 circuits = 3 shapes x 2 K arms: base / e_par / e_range, K=6 and K=12.
  e_par   = base + 1 parity row (sum h_j p_j = 0 mod q).
  e_range = base + per-coeff NumberCheck(1<<58).

GATES (circuit_size, from *_gates.json on disk)
  LEG        K    gates     PROVENANCE
  base       6    16,409    INHERITED (r137 w6; md5 == poc/r137/w6_gates.json)
  base      12    32,801    INHERITED (r137 w12; no fresh r141 base K=12 run)
  e_par      6    68,429    RAN fresh
  e_par     12   133,999    RAN fresh
  e_range    6   387,792  RAN fresh (re-run identical, md5-confirmed)
  e_range   12   772,824  RAN fresh (re-run identical, md5-confirmed)

PROVENANCE CORRECTION (honest read of the on-disk files)
  Only 4 circuits were freshly compiled this round: the e_par pair and the
  e_range pair. The two 'base' figures are the r137 committed anchors
  (base K=6 is byte-identical to ../r137/w6_gates.json; base K=12 has no
  r141 gate file at all). The base_run*.out logs are 0 bytes, so no fresh
  base recompile is preserved. This does NOT change the numbers: 16,409 and
  32,801 are the correct gate counts for the base cell at each K, and the
  e_range re-run identity shows this compiler is deterministic at the preset,
  so the base figures remain the right denominators.
  r142 MUST freshly re-compile base K=6 and base K=12 (with stdout captured)
  to convert the two inherited denominators into RAN-this-round.

DELTA (per-cell add = enhanced cell minus its base, same K)
  K=6 :  parity row  68,429 - 16,409 =   52,020 g   (4.17x base)
       range fam  387,792 - 16,409 =  371,383 g   (23.63x base)
  K=12:  parity row 133,999 - 32,801 =  101,198 g   (4.09x base)
       range fam 772,824 - 32,801 =  740,023 g   (23.56x base)
  (Delta over base: base legs are the inherited r137 anchors. e_par/e_range
   are RAN-fresh. The parity-vs-range ordering comes from two FRESH arms at
   the same K, so the ~5.7x spread RAN-holds independent of the base.)

HEADLINE (RAN-robust)
  The r140 acc-pin consumer cell is not kernel-closed on its own (r140).
  A parity row is the cheapest honest add and costs ~4.1x cell size; the
  dense per-coeff range family costs ~23.6x. The re-gate is NOT free.

VERDICT
  Option (a) sizing is RAN for the four enhanced cells. The parity-only
  "free re-gate" option framed in r140 is now quantified: it is ~4x the
  acc-pin cell, and the dense range family is ~5.7x more than that. The
  owner a-vs-b dial (consumer-side pin vs producer-side hard restate) gets a
  RAN number on the consumer side from this round.

ARTIFACTS
